<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raetian Limes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd–3rd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Raetian Limes was the fortified frontier of the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raetia">Raetia</a>, running about 166 kilometres from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> near Eining in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> west to its junction with the Upper Germanic Limes. Built from the 2nd century, it was later reinforced with a stone wall. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> abandoned it around 260, during the crisis of the third century, and it is now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div>
